Here's a `MauiProgram.cs` showing how to register everything:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

namespace MyMauiApp;

public static class MauiProgram
{
    public static MauiApp CreateMauiApp()
    {
        var builder = MauiApp.CreateBuilder();
        builder
            .UseMauiApp<App>()
            .ConfigureFonts(fonts =>
            {
                fonts.AddFont("OpenSans-Regular.ttf", "OpenSansRegular");
            });

        // HttpClient: singleton so connections are reused (avoids socket exhaustion)
        builder.Services.AddSingleton<HttpClient>();

        // DataService: singleton because it wraps HttpClient and holds no per-user state
        builder.Services.AddSingleton<IDataService, DataService>();

        // ViewModels: transient so each navigation gets a fresh instance with clean state
        builder.Services.AddTransient<MainViewModel>();
        builder.Services.AddTransient<DetailViewModel>();

        // Pages: transient so each navigation creates a new page bound to its own ViewModel
        builder.Services.AddTransient<MainPage>();
        builder.Services.AddTransient<DetailPage>();

#if DEBUG
        builder.Logging.AddDebug();
#endif

        return builder.Build();
    }
}
```

**Why each lifetime:**

| Registration | Lifetime | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `HttpClient` | **Singleton** | Reuses TCP connections; avoids socket exhaustion from repeated `new HttpClient()` |
| `IDataService` | **Singleton** | Stateless gateway to the API — one instance is enough and it holds the shared `HttpClient` |
| ViewModels | **Transient** | Each navigation should get a fresh VM with clean state (no stale data from a previous visit) |
| Pages | **Transient** | Pairs 1:1 with its ViewModel; a new page avoids rendering artifacts from a recycled UI |

**Key rule of thumb:** services that manage connections or caches → **singleton**. UI-bound objects (pages/VMs) that carry per-screen state → **transient**. Use **scoped** only when you need a shared instance within a single operation/request (more common in Blazor/web than MAUI).
